# Runtime logs — contain visitor emails + request lines; not source.
access.log
serve.log

# LLM-spend ingest bearer secrets (ARCH-152). The /ingest/llm-spend endpoint
# this file authenticated is retired (platform/decisions/0044); a stale copy
# may still sit on the deployed mini pending operator cleanup, so this entry
# stays as a guard against ever committing it.
ingest-tokens.json

# Build artifacts — both tier bundles are regenerated from the KB index by
# build.py on every serve.sh (re)start, so they're reproducible, large, and
# not worth versioning.
site/

# Python + macOS cruft
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# assets/generate_icons.py writes this on every run, for eyeballing the mark
# before committing regenerated PNGs — byte-identical to icon-512.png, so
# there's nothing to version once the review it was for is done.
/icon-preview.png

# Coverage outputs — produced by `pytest --cov` (CI uploads coverage.json as the
# `coverage` artifact; locally they're throwaway).
.coverage
coverage.json
htmlcov/

# Control-plane datastore (WS0.5, ARCH-348) — the operational DB lives outside
# the repo at ~/.orient-control/; these guard a stray local/CLI copy + WAL files.
control.db
control.db-wal
control.db-shm
.alembic-autogen.db

# Agent write-API bearer secrets (WS0.7) — per-agent tokens, like ingest-tokens.
# See api-tokens.example.json for the format.
#
# The glob covers the BACKUPS too, not just the file. Editing a credential file
# by hand means copying it aside first, and `api-tokens.json.bak-premint` was
# sitting untracked and unignored in this checkout on 2026-08-13 — one `git add
# -A` from being committed, with live bearer tokens in it. The example file is
# re-admitted below, since it is the one member of this glob that belongs here.
api-tokens.json*
!api-tokens.example.json

# Reading Room concierge Anthropic key (ARCH-357 fast-follow). {api_key, model}.
# Console-credit billed; read per-request, NEVER exported to the env (ARCH-146).
concierge.json

# Access control, read per request from ORIENT_CONFIG_ROOT: the Cloudflare
# Access binding (jwt.json), the full-tier list (tiers.json) and per-person
# roles (roles.json). They were tracked until issue_01M2RVJK4DDNJSGK5Y2AETKB43,
# which untracked them because a public export carries the tree and tiers.json
# names real people. Each has a committed .example template beside it, and
# tests/test_config_untracked.py fails if the real file is tracked again. The
# trailing glob covers hand-made backups, as with api-tokens.json above.
jwt.json*
tiers.json*
roles.json*

# Agent platform: .claude/ is individuated locally by `knowledge-ctx use <profile>`
# (agents, skills, settings) — regenerated on every dispatch, not committed. This
# repo has no root CLAUDE.md; if one is ever added it is outside this pattern and
# stays tracked.
.claude/

# Scratch input for a PR description. `agentctl pr-open` does NOT read this
# path: it reads `git rev-parse --git-path pr-body.md`, which in a worktree is
# .git/worktrees/<name>/pr-body.md — git metadata, never in the working tree and
# never committed. Write a PR body THERE, not here.
#
# This file was tracked until 2026-09-16, holding one old PR's description
# (216dea1) that nothing read. It cost something twice: a file named pr-body.md
# holding the wrong PR's body is a convincing explanation for a publishing trap
# that does not exist, and it produced one. And a coder writing its body at this
# intuitive path edits a tracked file, so the change lands in the diff — PR #302
# carried a 114-line pr-body.md change beside an unrelated removal, doing
# nothing.
#
# Ignored so the path stays available as scratch without either cost returning.
pr-body.md
